label: Parcel Identity
description: >-
  The resolved identity block of a parcel card -- blue-ribbon's
  `ParcelIdentity` (packages/schema/src/identity.ts). The output of the fan-in,
  and the end of this slice.

  The provenance here is the interesting part: it is `combineProvenance` over
  the parcel source and the township source, so a parcel whose geometry came
  direct from its county but whose township came from the statewide layer is
  only as trustworthy as the weaker of the two. That combine is a lattice meet,
  and it is the thing weir's classification propagation should BE.
fields:
  pin:
    classification: linkable
    type: utf8
    label: PIN
    description: Canonical dash-separated parcel identification number
    nullable: false
    validations:
      minLength: 8
      maxLength: 40
  county:
    type: utf8
    label: County
    description: The county this parcel is in
    nullable: false
    validations:
      minLength: 4
      maxLength: 20
  township:
    type: utf8
    label: Township
    description: The city or township containing the parcel
    nullable: false
    validations:
      minLength: 2
      maxLength: 100
  acres:
    type: f64
    label: Acres
    description: Parcel area in acres
    nullable: false
    validations:
      min: 0
      max: 100000
  boundaryJson:
    type: utf8
    label: Boundary JSON
    description: The parcel's polygon boundary, serialized GeoJSON
    nullable: false
    validations:
      minLength: 2
      maxLength: 2000000
  "...Provenanced":
